{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for \\(\\tan \\angle AMB\\) in a regular tetrahedron \\(ABCD\\) where \\(M\\) is the midpoint of \\(\\overline{CD}\\), we will use coordinate geometry and vector analysis.\n\nFirst, we place the tetrahedron in a 3-dimensional coordinate system. Assume each edge of the tetrahedron is of length \\(a\\). We can place the vertices as follows:\n- \\(A = (1, 1, 1)\\)\n- \\(B = (1, -1, -1)\\)\n- \\(C = (-1, 1, -1)\\)\n- \\(D = (-1, -1, 1)\\)\n\nThe midpoint \\(M\\) of \\(\\overline{CD}\\) is calculated as:\n\\[\nM = \\left( \\frac{-1 + (-1)}{2}, \\frac{1 + (-1)}{2}, \\frac{-1 + 1}{2} \\right) = (-1, 0, 0)\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{AM}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{BM}\\):\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{AM} = M - A = (-1 - 1, 0 - 1, 0 - 1) = (-2, -1, -1)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{BM} = M - B = (-1 - 1, 0 - (-1), 0 - (-1)) = (-2, 1, 1)\n\\]\n\nTo find \\(\\tan \\angle AMB\\), we use the dot product and magnitudes of these vectors. The dot product \\(\\overrightarrow{AM} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{BM}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{AM} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{BM} = (-2)(-2) + (-1)(1) + (-1)(1) = 4 - 1 - 1 = 2\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":1064,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,1124,11520,52591,1124,4044,6769,33,57758,304,264,5792,27853,32507,291,2248,17767,1867,6484,57758,1380,17767,44,57758,374,279,81963,315,1124,11520,1975,1056,90,6484,11035,701,582,686,990,16184,17047,323,4621,6358,382,5338,11,582,1992,279,27853,32507,291,2248,304,264,220,18,32420,16184,1849,13,62197,1817,6821,315,279,27853,32507,291,2248,374,315,3084,17767,64,59,568,1205,646,1992,279,17228,438,11017,510,12,17767,32,284,320,16,11,220,16,11,220,16,10699,340,12,17767,33,284,320,16,11,481,16,11,481,16,10699,340,12,17767,34,284,10293,16,11,220,16,11,481,16,10699,340,12,17767,35,284,10293,16,11,481,16,11,220,16,10699,692,785